# Veripsa release gate (auto-discovered). One gate per file -> two PRs adding gates add two FILES, never a
# shared line -> no false merge conflict on registration. register_gate is defined in run_gates.sh.
# Format: register_gate <test> <marker> <name> <ok_blurb> <desc> [tail]
register_gate "tests/test_config_key_cap.py" "CONFIG-KEY-CAP GATE: PASS" "config-key-cap silent-drop (schema-flood skip + per-file cap)" "config-key-cap: JSON Schema definition files (*.schema.json / *.tmLanguage.json / any JSON with a top-level dollar-schema key) and data-dump JSON files are no longer allowed to exhaust the config_key pool -- they carry zero cross-file app coupling but were minting thousands of structural vocabulary keys (properties.X.description / .type / ...) that silently dropped real coupling keys (env vars / app settings) processed later. The fix: (1) _is_json_schema_file skips schema files by suffix / exact basename / dollar-schema content; (2) _MAX_CONFIG_KEYS_PER_FILE=500 caps any single file so one data dump cannot consume the global pool; (3) _CONFIG_SKIP_FILES expanded to include pnpm-lock.yaml / yarn.lock / cargo.lock / go.sum / etc. Recall-positive overall: real app-coupling keys that were being crowded out now survive. MEASURED on nx: before=20000 nodes (cap exhausted) / 7553 reads_config edges; after=9803 nodes (well under cap) / 6169 reads_config edges; schema junk (properties.*) gone; real verdaccio config keys (max_body_size / fail_timeout / htpasswd) now minted." "config-key-cap HIGH SILENT-DROP fix: JSON Schema definition files and data-dump JSON (*.schema.json / schema.json / *.tmLanguage.json / dollar-schema content / lock files) no longer exhaust the 20k config_key pool -- a pool exhausted by schema floods caused real app env-var coupling keys processed later to be silently dropped (two files reading the same env var reported as UNRELATED). Per-file cap 500 + schema skip ensure every real config file contributes its keys regardless of walk order" 28
